WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.375
Scenario: A team shares a folder containing internal project

2
00:00:03.375 --> 00:00:06.750
documents through an anonymous link that never expires. The

3
00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.125
folder is no longer being actively used. Safest response:

4
00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:13.500
Option A: Restrict access to named authorized accounts, set

5
00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:16.875
an expiry/review date and remove obsolete access. Restrict identities

6
00:00:16.875 --> 00:00:20.625
and duration, and review existing permissions according to data sensitivity.

7
00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:24.000
Option B is unsafe because A folder name does

8
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:27.375
not change who can access its content. Option C

9
00:00:27.375 --> 00:00:30.750
is unsafe because Wider distribution increases exposure and does

10
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.125
not establish authorization. Option D is unsafe because Convenience

11
00:00:34.125 --> 00:00:37.500
does not justify indefinite anonymous access. In practice: Remove

12
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.875
anonymous access, grant only necessary users or groups, set

13
00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:44.250
expiry where available and periodically review permissions. Key takeaway:

14
00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.625
Cloud sharing should be identity-bound, least-privilege and time-limited when

15
00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:48.000
appropriate.
